# 🚩 Challenge: [GDB baby step 1]
![alt text](gdb_bs_1.png)
## 📝 Challenge Description
Can you figure out what is in the eax register at the end of the main function? Put your answer in the academy flag format: academy{n} where n is the contents of the eax register in the decimal number base. If the answer was 0x11 your flag would be academy{17}. Disassemble this
.

Hints
1. gdb is a very good debugger to use for this problem and many others!

2. main is actually a recognized symbol that can be used with gdb commands.


### Code / Terminal Snippets
```bash
1. wget https://challenge-files.cylabacademy.net/library/03b038548e2a34973bde05a78fadc1f09467a1d03ffbfb9e4b48bd44e87c0e70/debugger0_a
2. gdb debugger0_a
3. disassemble main
4. print(str(0x86342))
```

---

## 🚀 Exploitation / Solution Path
Detail your step-by-step breakdown to get the flag:
1. Download the challenge file using `wget`.
2. Debug the file code with `gdb` and `disassemble` the code with main.
3. The hexadecimal value will be shown in `eax`.
4. Convert the hexadecimal value to decimal using `cyberchef`.
5. After conversion it is the flag.

